+    "command": "set -euo pipefail\nREPLAY_ROOT=\"/tmp/practice05-framework-replay-20261102\"\ncd \"$REPLAY_ROOT\"\n# Stage 2: Constitution\ncat > feature/studyspace-deadline-move/spec/constitution.md << 'EOF'\n# Project Constitution — UI Quality Principles\n\n- Prioritize clarity, consistency, and responsiveness in UI components.\n- Use accessible markup and ARIA roles; ensure keyboard operability.\n- Preserve existing design system styles and component patterns.\n- Validate inputs locally and surface friendly, actionable errors.\n- Avoid implicit data mutations; UI change should not auto-alter task status.\n- Treat dates in Moscow time for display and overdue cues.\n- Keep modal interactions non-destructive; cancel always restores prior state.\nEOF\n\n# Stage 2: Specification (summarize feature intent; UI-only)\ncat > feature/studyspace-deadline-move/spec/spec.md << 'EOF'\n# Feature Specification — StudySpace Deadline Move (UI-only)\n\nGoal: Allow a user to change a task's deadline using a modal dialog, with clear rules and feedback.\n\nUser Story:\n- As a student, I want to open a task's deadline modal, select a new date, and save it so my schedule updates.\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n- A date-edit affordance opens a modal titled \"Перенос дедлайна\".\n- Modal shows task title and current deadline in Moscow time (ru-RU, full date).\n- Date input (type=date) prefilled; requires YYYY-MM-DD; invalid blocks save.\n- Past dates allowed; today is not treated overdue.\n- If the chosen date equals the current deadline, show hint and disable Save.\n- Saving calls the update deadline API; on success: modal closes, list refreshes, toast.\n- Errors are normalized in Russian; modal stays open.\n- Done tasks remain done; status is not changed.\n- UI locks mode switch while modal is open.\nEOF\n\n# Stage 2: Clarify — capture invariants and decisions\ncat > feature/studyspace-deadline-move/spec/clarify.md << 'EOF'\n# Clarify — Agreed Invariants\n\n- Allowed dates: past dates permitted; today counts as not overdue.\n- Same-date: Save is disabled; no request is sent.\n- Status: tasks in 'done' remain unchanged by deadline edits.\n- Mode: data mode (real/demo) is locked while modal is open.\n- Calendar/timezone: Moscow time governs display and overdue cues.\n- Error normalization: server English messages can be normalized to Russian in UI.\nEOF\n\n# Stage 2: Plan — UI-only plan (no backend edits)\ncat > feature/studyspace-deadline-move/plan/plan.md << 'EOF'\n# Plan — UI Implementation (React)\n\nScope: UI-only additions in the existing dashboard.\n\nComponents:\n- Date-edit button in task row triggers opening state (deadlineTask).\n- Modal (dialog) titled \"Перенос дедлайна\" with summary of task and current deadline.\n- Input: HTML date field bound to local state; prefilled; validation for YYYY-MM-DD.\n- States: saving flag; error string; same-date detection; invalid flag.\n- Actions: Cancel (close) and Save (submit).\n- API call: POST /api/tools/update_task_deadline?mode={real|demo} with {task_id, deadline}.\n- UX: Disable Save when invalid or same as current; show spinner on Save; lock mode switch while modal is open.\n- Toast on success; error banner normalized on failure.\n\nNo backend code changes in this stage. Backend contract is owned by OpenSpec.\nEOF\n\n# Stage 2: Tasks — actionable steps (UI-only, no code execution here)\ncat > feature/studyspace-deadline-move/tasks/tasks.md << 'EOF'\n# Tasks — UI-only\n\nSetup:\n- Review current dashboard styles and modal component patterns.\n\nFoundational:\n- Add date-edit affordance in task row (no functional change yet).\n- Create modal component skeleton with title, summary, and date input.\n\nUser Story — Deadline Move:\n- Bind date input to state; prefill with current deadline.\n- Implement validation (YYYY-MM-DD), same-date detection, and disable Save accordingly.\n- Wire Save to API call (POST /api/tools/update_task_deadline?mode=...); handle success (close+refresh+toast) and failure (inline error).\n- Ensure mode lock while modal is open.\n- Preserve status 'done'; do not change task status.\n\nPolish:\n- Accessibility pass (focus management, role=alert for errors).\n- Localization and date display consistency (ru-RU, Moscow time).\nEOF\n\n# Stage 2: Analyze — initial consistency notes\ncat > feature/studyspace-deadline-move/analysis/analyze.md << 'EOF'\n# Analyze — Consistency Check\n\nArtifacts reviewed: constitution.md, spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md.\n\nFindings:\n- Requirements and plan align on UI-only scope; no backend edits implied.\n- API endpoint and body consistent across spec and plan; idempotent same-date noted.\n- Tasks reflect acceptance criteria including validation and error handling.\n- No contradictions found between invariants and task list.\nEOF\n\n# Stage 2: Contract — agreed API\ncat > practices/practice_05/frameworks/contract.yaml << 'EOF'\nendpoint: \"/api/tools/update_task_deadline\"\nquery:\n  mode: [\"real\", \"demo\"]\nmethod: \"POST\"\nbody:\n  type: object\n  required: [\"task_id\", \"deadline\"]\n  properties:\n    task_id: { type: integer }\n    deadline: { type: string, pattern: \"^\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}$\" }\nresponses:\n  200:\n    description: Raw MCP envelope; success confirmed by server; UI refreshes state.\n  400:\n    description: MCP validation or bridge body error; normalize to Russian UI message.\n  403:\n    description: Host Origin error; access or origin mismatch.\n  502:\n    description: MCP unavailable; network/service error.\nsemantics:\n  idempotent_same_date: true\n  ui_modal_save_blocked_if_unchanged: true\n  moscow_calendar: true\n  mode_locked_while_modal_open: true\nnotes:\n  - Other fields in state are preserved on success; UI GET state after save.\n  - Error messages can be normalized to Russian; server may return English.\nEOF\n\n# Stage 2: Negotiation UI decisions\ncat > practices/practice_05/frameworks/negotiation.ui.md << 'EOF'\n# Negotiation — UI Decisions\n\n- Adopted API: POST /api/tools/update_task_deadline?mode=real|demo with JSON {task_id, deadline}.\n- Idempotency: same-date results in no-op; UI blocks Save.\n- Error normalization: UI presents Russian messages; English server strings can be mapped.\n- Timezone: Moscow time for display and overdue cues.\n- Mode behavior: mode switching disabled while modal is open.\n- Status invariant: done tasks remain done; deadline change does not alter status.\nEOF\n",
